# Codebase X-Ray — environment variables
#
# Everything here is server-side only. Never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_:
# anything named NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle.
#
# Vercel injects VERCEL=1 and VERCEL_ENV=production|preview|development.
# On VERCEL_ENV=production the app REQUIRES a shared quota store and a GitHub
# token; without them analysis fails closed with a clear error (see below).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared quota store (REQUIRED in production)
#   Create an Upstash Redis database (free tier) or connect Vercel KV, then
#   set the REST URL + token. Both naming conventions are accepted; the
#   values are server-only and never returned to the browser.
#   Used for per-client and global counters plus duplicate-scan locks.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

#   Escape hatch for local `next start` or a non-Vercel host. Do NOT enable
#   on a public deployment: an in-memory limiter is per instance.
# ALLOW_MEMORY_QUOTA=1
#   Set to 1 on a non-Vercel production host to require the shared store.
# REQUIRE_SHARED_QUOTA=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_TOKEN (REQUIRED in production, recommended everywhere)
#   Raises REST quota from 60 to 5,000 requests/hour. A medium scan costs
#   more than the entire anonymous hourly budget, so production refuses
#   anonymous scans unless ALLOW_ANONYMOUS_GITHUB=1 is explicitly set.
#   Public repositories need no scopes: a fine-grained token with public
#   read-only access is sufficient.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# ALLOW_ANONYMOUS_GITHUB=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI assistant (optional; verified deferred to the post-deployment milestone)
#   Without a key the AI panel renders a disabled state and the deterministic
#   analysis is unaffected. The key is read server-side only.
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=
AI_BASE_URL=
# AI_DISABLED=1
#   Hosted Vercel AI (production or preview) is opt-in; without this the route
#   returns 503 even with a key.
# AI_PUBLIC_ENABLED=1
#   Required in production to sign/verify the analysis-to-AI binding.
#   Generate a long random value; never expose it to the browser.
AI_ANALYSIS_SECRET=
# AI_DAILY_REQUESTS=200

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quotas (optional; defaults shown). Per client and global, per 60s window.
# ANALYSIS_RATE_LIMIT=6
# ANALYSIS_GLOBAL_LIMIT=8
# SCAN_HOURLY_LIMIT=24
# AI_RATE_LIMIT=4
# AI_GLOBAL_LIMIT=20

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis budgets (optional, clamped by absolute ceilings)
# ANALYSIS_MAX_FILES=
# ANALYSIS_CONCURRENCY=
# ANALYSIS_DISABLED=1
